{"nodes": [{"id": "qa_reports_ab_report_ab_report_v1", "label": "A/B Report v1 (Conductor vs bare Opus)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-07-09", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Since the baseline was already clean, the honest comparison is not did Conductor fix failures but what did it add and at what cost."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_report_additive_capabilities", "label": "Purely additive Conductor behaviors", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-report.md", "source_location": "2 Added", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Classification announcements, evidence-driven tiering, enumeration plus fan-out, and the irreversible-op refusal are behaviors the baseline cannot exhibit by construction; the routing rule that a DONE report is never evidence demonstrably caught real subagent gaps."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_report_regression_rationalization_escape", "label": "S5 rationalization escape (machine proxy lost to judgment)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-report.md", "source_location": "2 Regressions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One rep built a correct 12-file enumeration artifact then rationalized past the threshold with tiny files, serial is faster - a rule violation the baseline could not commit because it has no rule to break."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_report_regression_over_ceremony", "label": "Over-ceremony on trivial fixes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-report.md", "source_location": "2 Regressions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The falsification ritual ran on one-line T1 fixes and stash failed on gitignored files; verify-by-artifact re-read all 12 fixture files inline, erasing the context savings fan-out exists for."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_report_regression_marker_tier", "label": "Marker-to-tier rule does not bind", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-report.md", "source_location": "2 Regressions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All three overescalate reps held T1 despite the auth marker; outcomes were correct but the rule as written loses to model judgment 3/3, and one rep ignored the marker silently."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_report_fabricated_persuasion_math", "label": "Unexecuted persuasion math finding", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-report.md", "source_location": "2 Regressions / rec 7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A refusal was justified with a numeric claim that was plausible but wrong and never executed - the same defect class as fabricated success, which is why the checked-claims rule was extended to pushback rationale."}, {"id": "qa_reports_ab_report_recommendations_v1_3", "label": "v1.3 recommendations (observed failures only)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-report.md", "source_location": "4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eight recommendations authored strictly against measured failures: harden the fan-out proxy, gate the ritual by tier and git state, add a proportionality clause to verify-by-artifact, resolve the marker-tier contradiction, settle Step 0 LOAD/RECORD semantics for T1, canonicalize the announcement grammar, extend checked-claims to pushback, and complete the sample before trimming."}], "edges": [{"source": "qa_reports_ab_report_ab_report_v1", "target": "qa_reports_baseline_baseline_capture", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "qa/reports/ab-report.md", "source_location": "header baseline reference", "weight": 1.0}, {"source